//! `fleet.install`: install or upgrade `legion` on a remote machine using only `ssh` and `scp`.
//!
//! Nothing a caller supplies is ever placed on a remote command line: probing, directory creation,
//! atomic replacement, permission updates, and cleanup all use fixed remote command shapes whose
//! only variable part is a temporary filename generated by Legion itself from the OS CSPRNG.
//!
//! All network, SSH, SCP, and post-install session verification operations pass through one small
//! trait ([`InstallBackend`]) so tests exercise every code path against an in-memory fake without
//! opening any real connection.

